🔥 WAKE-UP CALL

You can’t boil the ocean. Focus on the 3-5 perspectives that’ll make/break your system—or risk death by "what about-ism".




🔥 Why Perspectives? The Wake-Up Call

    Views tell you what the system is.

    Perspectives ensure it’s fast, secure, and unbreakable.

    Without them: Congrats, you’ve built a functionally correct house of cards.

Example:

    Your Functional View shows a flawless checkout flow.

    Your Performance Perspective reveals it crashes at 100 users. Oops.


💡 Perspectives vs. Viewpoints: Clarity in 10 Seconds
Concept	Role	Output
Viewpoint	"How to document"	Clean diagrams (e.g., deployment maps)
Perspective	"How to harden"	Upgraded design (e.g., auto-scaling + encryption)

Key Move: Apply perspectives iteratively—test, tweak, repeat.




🎯 How to Use Perspectives Like a Pro

    Pick Your Battles

        Not all perspectives matter equally. Prioritize:

            E-commerce? Security + Performance + Availability.

            Internal tool? Evolution + Development.

    Stress-Test Your Views

        Security Perspective → Audit Functional View for auth gaps.

        Performance Perspective → Simulate load on Deployment View.

    Document the Wins

        Keep only critical artifacts (threat models, load tests).

        Toss the rest (no one needs 37 drafts of a meeting note).




